  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 813 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge over much of the central and southeastern \nUS will persist into this weekend; however, it looks like an upper\ntrough tries to dig south over the Northeast, potentially \nbreaking down the ridge over the Appalachians, Ohio Valley, and \nTennessee Valley somewhat during this time. This may be short-\nlived, since synoptic guidance suggests that the ridge will build \nback over the Southeast through early next week. At the surface, \nhigh pressure over the Appalachians may be overtaken by a backdoor\ncold front slated to move into the region from the northeast by \nSunday. Some guidance hints that this feature may bring enough \nmoisture and lift with it to produce at least a low chance of \nshowers and storms this weekend, but these trends will be \nmonitored. By early next week, surface high pressure builds back \nover the Appalachians as the upper ridge takes hold over the \nregion once again.\n\nOverall, the hot and humid conditions are expected to continue \nthrough the long term period. Expect highs in the mid to upper 90s\nthrough the weekend with not much relief at night as lows merely \ndip into the upper 60s to lower 70s. These temperatures, along \nwith dew points in the lower to mid 70s, will result in heat \nindices in the 100-106 degree range along with WBGTs in the mid to\nupper 80s (some spots around 90 degrees) and Moderate to Major \nHeatRisk (levels 2 and 3 of 4) for most of north Alabama and \nsouthern middle Tennessee. By early next week, the aforementioned \nbackdoor front may temper the heat and humidity slightly. Highs in\nthe lower to mid 90s with dew points in the upper 60s to lower \n70s are anticipated, keeping the HeatRisk in the Moderate Risk \ncategory, heat indices generally between 98-103 degrees, and WBGTs\nsolidly in the 83-87 degree range. Ultimately, the current Heat \nAdvisory runs through Saturday evening; however, we will be \nmonitoring if a further extension into Sunday becomes necessary.\n\nRemember to practice heat safety, especially if you work outside \nor have outdoor activities! Stay hydrated, take plenty of breaks \nin the shade, and never leave people or pets in vehicles!",
